# Prefer the workspace layout and shared crates
- Use crates/shared-redis for Redis key helpers.
- Use crates/shared-core for symbols, discriminators, and canonical pair logic.
- Do not duplicate Redis key strings; import from shared-redis.

# Keep binaries separated
- Geyser subscriber lives in crates/geyser-producer (thin, reliable).
- Heavy parsing/normalization lives in crates/dex-data-parser (scalable).
- One-off tools and backfill live in crates/ops-tools/src/bin/*.

# Safety
- Do not edit idls/* in-place; if changing IDL, mirror into versioned path or use include_str!.
- No network keys or secrets in code. Use .env and env! only for non-secrets.

# Style
- Run cargo fmt and cargo clippy –deny warnings.
